  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Granny Sha recounts that Heavenly Court has owned Fixed Immortal Travel multiple times. Once it was in the hands of Heavenly Court Gu Immortal Liang Liang, who raised it to rank seven. He cultivated space path alone, but during the rampage of immemorial desolate beasts he battled and died, and that rank seven Fixed Immortal Travel was destroyed.",
      "chapters": [
        1069
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_granny_sha",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He was famous in history as a rank eight Gu Immortal from Heavenly Court and a space path expert. Months before Lang Ya blessed land is breached, Fairy Zi Wei uses the method he left behind and awakens his final will. With that will’s help, Heavenly Court raises Fixed Immortal Travel to rank seven again and creates the immortal killer move seven immortal doors. When Feng Jiu Ge and the other Central Continent Gu Immortals arrive, that remnant will dissipates after reaching its limit, and Fang Yun Hua sighs that Senior Liang Liang’s final remaining will has been destroyed.",
      "chapters": [
        1540
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
